To make a component skip re-rendering when its props have not changed, you can wrap the component in `memo`. This tells React that the component should not re-render as long as its props remain the same. Here is an example:

```js
const Greeting = memo(function Greeting({ name }) {
  return <h1>Hello, {name}!</h1>;
});
```

By using `memo`, React will only re-render the component if its props change, adhering to the requirement of pure rendering logic [1].

